# Credentials — never commit. See docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md for the required keys.
# The glob matters: ops/switch_broker.py writes config/.env.switch_broker.bak,
# which is a byte copy of config/.env and therefore carries the same secrets.
config/.env
config/.env.*
.env
deploy/ibgw/.env

# Market data (3.8 GB). Rebuilt with the scripts in scripts/fetch/.
# See docs/INFRASTRUCTURE.md section "Rebuilding the data folder".
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING (fixed 2026-09-10): a bare `data/` also
# matched src/data/, silently untracking r2.py and __init__.py, and would
# swallow any future src/**/data/ module the same way.
/data/

# Caches and scratch
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
results/**/_cache_*
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Live broker state — machine-specific, regenerated each session
ops/books/**/_desync/
ops/logs/
*.log

# Live ledgers and heartbeat — STATE, not code.
# Tracking these made prod's tree permanently dirty (every session writes them),
# so ops/promote.sh had to exclude them by pathspec and check out with --merge
# just to get past its own "clean tree" gate. A governance gate that has to be
# weakened to pass is not a gate. They come out of git; ops/backup_state.sh is
# what replaces the commit history as their off-machine copy, which is why
# untracking is gated on that job actually being SCHEDULED — until then git is
# their only backup.
# Untrack (human runs this, in the DEV tree, then tag and promote — see below):
#   git rm -r --cached ops/books/cef_live ops/books/benchmarks_live \
#                      ops/books/phase0_live ops/heartbeat.json
# NOT in the prod worktree: prod is detached at a tag, so a commit there is
# dangling. Untrack in dev, commit, tag, promote — prod then checks out a tree
# in which they were never tracked.
ops/books/cef_live/
ops/books/benchmarks_live/
ops/books/phase0_live/
ops/heartbeat.json

# Rendered launchd plists — machine-specific absolute paths, so committing them
# is how ops/schedule/rendered/*.plist came to point at a repo path that has not
# existed since 2026-08-31 while still looking authoritative (CLAUDE.md landmine
# #2). The TEMPLATE is the tracked artifact; the render is local output.
ops/schedule/rendered_backup/
